  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elbitamerica obligated $358M in FY2026 to date across 178 awards, with an average award size of $2M. Obligations are up 359.5% year over year. The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $306M, followed by the Department of Defense with $51.5M. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is the largest market, with $316M in obligations. Historical obligations show year-to-year movement: FY21 $115M, FY22 $119M, FY23 $96.8M, FY24 $137M, FY25 $77.9M, and FY26 $358M. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). This profile highlights where federal spending for Elbitamerica is concentrated by agency and NAICS market and how FY2026 to date compares to prior fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying from Elbitamerica?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $306M from Elbitamerica in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $51.5M. The Department of Transportation obligated $0."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which product and service markets drive Elbitamerica obligations?",
        "body": "Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounted for $316M in obligations. Other notable markets include All Other Miscellaneous General Purpose Machinery Manufacturing with $14.4M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing with $10.9M. Remaining markets in FY2026 to date include Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance $4.5M and Electronic Computer Manufacturing $2.2M among others."
      }
    ]
  },
